Design a circuit for an Error Correction Coding (ECC) memory block that processes an incoming data signal consisting of 8 bits and outputs a 16-bit memory format. The module calculates four check bits based on specific combinations of the input data bits using XOR operations to provide error detection capabilities. It then organizes the processed data bits and computed check bits into a structured output format for storage, helping to ensure data integrity in memory applications. This functionality is critical for applications requiring reliable data transmission and retrieval in the presence of potential errors.
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] data_in,
  output reg [m-1:0] mem_out // Change to reg type
