description:
Design a synchronous circuit that processes a 126-bit input signal (a) and produces a single-bit output (q). On each clock cycle, the input is stored in a register (g_r), and a selection signal (sel) is derived from the lower 7 bits of the input. The circuit extends the stored value by appending a 1 and a 0 to create a 128-bit wire (g_extend). The output q is determined by the bit in g_extend specified by the sel signal, effectively acting as a bit selector based on the input.
module top_module(
   input clk,
   input [125:0] a,
   output reg q
   );

code:
module top_module(
   input clk,
   input [125:0] a,
   output reg q
   );reg [125:0] g_r;

   wire [127:0] g_extend = { g_r, 1'b1, 1'b0 };

   reg [6:0] sel;
   wire g_sel = g_extend[sel];

   always @ (posedge clk) begin
      g_r <= a;
      sel <= a[6:0];
      q <= g_sel;
   end

endmodule

